bhaṭṭāra, m. [Pr. for strg. base of 🞄bhartṛ], N. of various men: -ka, m. lord, 🞄venerable or worshipful person (used of gods, 🞄men of rank, or scholars);
 kind of Śaiva-monk;
 🞄-maṭha, m. (conj.) N. of a college;
 🞄-vāra, m. day of the Lord, Sunday;
 -āyatana, n. house of the Lord, temple.
